From: Nadia Rodionova <273119990+sosidudku1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:02:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(fusion): label workers on a foreign llama.cpp server
 with the model it serves (ATO-1562)

A llama.cpp server that is not the agent's own holds one loaded model
and ignores the model a request names, so llm.runMode.fusion.workerModel
picked nothing there: worker rows named the pick (or the managed model,
which runs somewhere else) while another model answered.

fusion.delegate now asks such a server what it serves (GET /props,
model_alias else the model file name) and labels the worker rows, the
fan-out line and pricing with it. When the person picked a different
model, the fan-out's result says so once per session: "Selected X, but
the server serves Y. The model is changed on the server side." The main
local server keeps its label, and a server that does not answer keeps
the pick as before.

(cherry picked from commit f0c5d5da2e81224ac5c0d746125b94396e77c7a2)
