Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(tui): no model pick for a foreign llama.cpp server in
 the Fusion composer (ATO-1563)

The composer's model switch for a Fusion leg on a llama.cpp server that
is not the agent's own listed catalog rows whose pick only wrote a
label: that server serves the model it loaded whatever a request names.
It now shows one row, "Loaded on the server: X" (or just "Loaded on the
server" when the entry names no model), which cannot be chosen and says
to change the model on the server. The orchestrator also refuses such a
pick if it arrives by another path.

LM Studio, Ollama and cloud providers keep their model lists; with the
per-turn role model from ATO-1560 a pick there is what the leg runs.
The built-in local model switches as before.

(cherry picked from commit 4ac920e76a8c4388e90b7984cd169d1849064c24)
